==English==
{{rft}}
{{wikipedia|Styx (mythology)}}

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|Στύξ|lang=grc|tr=Stux}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/stɪks/|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|lang=en|sticks}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{context|Greek mythology|lang=en}} The river, in [[Hades]], over which the [[soul]]s of the dead are [[ferried]] by [[Charon]].
# {{context|astronomy|lang=en}} The 5th [[moon]] of [[Pluto]], discovered in 2012.
====Derived terms====
* [[stygian]]

====Coordinate terms====
* [[Acheron]], [[Cocytus]], [[Eridanos]], [[Lethe]], [[Phlegethon]]

